# Price-time priority: better prices trade first, and at the same price, earlier orders trade first.
> add ACME
added ACME
> buy 100 @ 100.00
ACME #1 BUY 100 @ 100.00 -> resting 100
> buy 50 @ 100.00
ACME #2 BUY 50 @ 100.00 -> resting 50
> buy 70 @ 100.25
ACME #3 BUY 70 @ 100.25 -> resting 70
> book
ACME  CONTINUOUS  last -  resting 3
              BID                       ASK
     100.25 x 70      (1)
     100.00 x 150     (2)

# A sell for 200 takes the best bid at 100.25 first, then the two bids at 100.00 in the order they arrived.
# Every trade happens at the resting order's price.
> sell 200 @ 99.50
ACME #4 SELL 200 @ 99.50 -> filled 200
  trade #1  70 @ 100.25  buy #3  sell #4
  trade #2  100 @ 100.00  buy #1  sell #4
  trade #3  30 @ 100.00  buy #2  sell #4
> book
ACME  CONTINUOUS  last 100.00  resting 1
              BID                       ASK
     100.00 x 20      (1)
> trades
  trade #3  30 @ 100.00  buy #2  sell #4
  trade #2  100 @ 100.00  buy #1  sell #4
  trade #1  70 @ 100.25  buy #3  sell #4
